.TH SDL_ThreadState 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_ThreadState \- The SDL thread state.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_thread.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef enum SDL_ThreadState
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_THREAD_UNKNOWN,     /**< The thread is not valid */
.BI "    SDL_THREAD_ALIVE,       /**< The thread is currently running */
.BI "    SDL_THREAD_DETACHED,    /**< The thread is detached and can't be waited on */
.BI "    SDL_THREAD_COMPLETE     /**< The thread has finished and should be cleaned up with SDL_WaitThread() */
.BI "} SDL_ThreadState;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The current state of a thread can be checked by calling
.BR SDL_GetThreadState \[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This enum is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetThreadState (3)
